# SCENARIO: p5_human_cast_reload_off   SEED: 0   CAMERAS: auto   BOTCFG: auto
# #163: a human cast that is running when allowPlayerCast goes true -> false (config reload) stops
# within a second (Player::onThink): the caster is told, the viewer is disconnected and the
# cast_broadcasters row is withdrawn (no orphan). Needs an external driver that, once the row
# exists, sets allowPlayerCast = false in config.lua and queues `_global reloadconfig`
# (.work/cast163/reload_driver.py). Starts with allowPlayerCast = true.
@p1 login
@p1 goto 32369,32220,7 range=1 stuck=10 timeout=120
@p1 say /cast off
@p1 hold 2
@p1 say /cast on
@srv db "SELECT p.name FROM cast_broadcasters c JOIN players p ON p.id = c.player_id WHERE p.name = 'Harness One'" expect="Harness One" wait=20
@cam:$CASTER login desc=@cast pw=
@cam:$CASTER perceive reset=1
@p1 hold 25
@srv expect src=cli:p1 k=see_msg text~="Player cast has been disabled on this server" min=1 within=120
@srv expect src=cli:c1 k=game_end min=1 within=120 wait=25
@srv db "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cast_broadcasters c JOIN players p ON p.id = c.player_id WHERE p.name = 'Harness One'" expect="^0" wait=25
@srv expect src=srv msg~="\[Cast\] Harness One: cast stopped, allowPlayerCast is now false" min=1 within=180
@p1 say /cast on
@p1 hold 3
@srv expect src=cli:p1 k=see_msg text~="Player cast is disabled on this server" min=1 within=30
@p1 logout
